\\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class = \\\"strong\\\">Expressing Simple Requests</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class = \\\"strong\\\">Offering help</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class = \\\"italic\\\">Can you ... please?<br/>Could you ... ?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class = \\\"italic\\\">How can I help you?<br/>What can I get you?\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class = \"strong\">Helena</span>: Can you send that letter please?<br/><span class = \"strong\">Tim</span>: Uh-huh, sure."}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class = \"strong\">Clerk</span>: What can I get you?<br/><span class = \"strong\">Mike</span>: Could I have the tuna special, please?"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Using Sounds and Expressions to Show You Are Listening"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "It is important to show that you understand when someone asks you a question.<br/>Use the following sounds and expressions to show you are listening."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":\"2\",\"columns\":\"2\",\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class = \\\"strong\\\">Expressions</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class = \\\"strong\\\">Sounds</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Alright<br/>Okay<br/>Sure\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"hmm-hmm<br/>uh-huh\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class = \"strong\">Helena</span>: Can you send that letter please?<br/><span class = \"strong\">Tim</span>: Uh-huh, sure."}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class = \"strong\">Helena</span>: Could I have the tuna special, please?<br/><span class = \"strong\">Tim</span>: Hmm-hmm, alright."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "deli"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a store selling prepared foods like sandwiches, salads, and drinks"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: This deli has great sandwiches."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le06ob07aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use when you talk about food."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "delicious"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "very nice to eat"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The tuna special is my favorite. It's delicious!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le06ob07aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "gross"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "not nice to eat (informal)"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Pickles are gross! How can you eat them?!?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le06ob07aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "pickles"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "vegetables, like cucumbers, you put in vinegar for a long time"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Can I have extra pickles in my sandwiches please?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le06ob07aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "sandwich"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "two slices of bread with filling between them, like cheese or meat"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The tuna sandwich is my favorite."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le06ob07aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "soda"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a sweet, carbonated drink"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Can I have two sodas with my sandwich please?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le06ob07aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "tuna"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a large fish"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I love tuna. It's my favorite kind of fish."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn2le06ob07aud07"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn2le06ob07re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Write a dialogue with your partner of 20 - 30 words."}, {"type": "text", "content": "In the dialogue, write about food and your favorite kind of sandwich."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Place an order. You are the customer. Be polite."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you are the clerk, show you are listening."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I write a dialogue about favorite foods."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I use sounds and expressions to show I am listening."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I ask for permission."}]}], "type": "sena"}